  Rule: "pass 6\u2019s cut over x 98.8 to 113.8, y 55.0 to 69.4 (SCHEMA: the ground
    change round the fall): the fan eased, the channel above the lip, the pool\u2019s
    bowl and the chute, blended into the ground round it over its last 1.6 m; and,
    where pass 9\u2019s shore stands 1.5 to 2 m under part 1\u2019s bank north of
    the pool, a shingle bar on the pool\u2019s north rim (crest +2.25, its outer
    face 0.45 m a metre down to pass 9\u2019s beach, notched to +2.03 at the spill)
    so the pool holds as drawn. Laid on Ginny\u2019s plan ground without the Fen
    Pool\u2019s fill, which is pass 9 (the second issue s2.1). At the run\u2019s
    head, the Fen Pool\u2019s sill: in the outlet\u2019s sector of the pool\u2019s
    rim (28 deg either side of the run\u2019s line, in the pool\u2019s own frame),
    between 1.03 and 1.15 of its radius, its crest +5.25 at the run\u2019s line (106.93,
    55.3) rising 0.15 m to the sector\u2019s ends, its faces 1 in 1; only raises.
    With it the bowl holds the fen at +5.25, as pass 9 plans it and the ruled boards
    draw it"
